---
components: ["ResendCodeButton"]
description: Resend code buttons let users request a new verification code, with a cooldown after each request so codes are not sent in a burst.
---

<script>
  import { PinCodeInput, ResendCodeButton, Stack } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

## Default

The cooldown starts on mount, since the page usually sends a code just before it renders. The button counts down, then dispatches `on:resend` when clicked and starts the cooldown again. During the cooldown the button stays focusable and ignores clicks, so keyboard focus does not jump away after a resend.

<Stack gap={5}>
  <PinCodeInput count={6} labelText="Verification code" />
  <ResendCodeButton
    cooldown={10}
    on:resend={() => console.log("resend")}
  />
</Stack>

## Available on mount

Set `startOnMount` to `false` to make the button available right away.

<ResendCodeButton startOnMount={false} cooldown={10} />

## Custom cooldown

Set `cooldown` to the number of seconds to wait after each resend. The default is `30`. Set it to `0` to disable the cooldown.

<ResendCodeButton cooldown={60} />

## Custom text

Set `labelText` for the available state and `cooldownText` to format the countdown, for example to translate it.

<ResendCodeButton
  cooldown={10}
  labelText="Reenviar código"
  cooldownText={(seconds) => `Reenviar en ${seconds}s`}
/>

## Cancel the cooldown

`on:resend` is cancelable. Call `e.preventDefault()` when the code could not be sent, and the button stays available.

```svelte
<ResendCodeButton
  on:resend={(e) => {
    if (!sendCode()) e.preventDefault();
  }}
/>
```

## Programmatic usage

Use `bind:this` to call the component's methods, and bind `remaining` to read the seconds left.

| Method | Description | Signature |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `start` | Start or restart the cooldown. | `() => void` |
| `reset` | End the cooldown so a resend is available now. | `() => void` |
